The '''León Company''' ({{Langx|bl|Compañía León}}; {{langx|mxi|Compañía Liyún|lit=Lion Company}}) is a prominent [[w:Cooperative federation|cooperative federation]] in [[Balisca]], primarily known for its extensive role in [[W:Urban planning|urban planning]], housing, and infrastructure development. Since its founding in the 1950s, the federation has spearheaded the continuous development of [[León]], a planned [[W:Satellite city|satellite city]] that has become an integral part of the [[Concordia|Concordia conurbation]].

== History ==
=== Founding and early development (1950s) ===
[[File:León bridge.png|left|thumb|300px|[[Ponte de León|Pont de León]] ("Lion's Bridge"), developed by the Compañía León.]]
Compañía León was established in the 1950s, a period coinciding with Balisca's "[[Baliscan economic miracle|economic miracle]]" and ambitious post-[[W:World War II|World War II]] urban development plans. The cooperative federation was founded to address the growing demand for housing and planned urban spaces, particularly as millions of people migrated to Balisca's cities. Its initial project was the comprehensive development of León, a new satellite city located in the [[Araucaria|Araucarian region]] of [[Tukupi]], on the banks of the [[Coroado River]]. This development was part of the broader confederal effort championed by confederal figures like [[Saqr Hanania]] and [[Pasqual Sargata]] to construct "satisfactory housing" and manage urban growth.

From its inception, Compañía León adopted a steady pace of development, characterized by a commitment to planned communities that integrated housing with essential infrastructure and public services.

